// Resource script for AyaanCursors.dll, a resource-only DLL holding nothing but
// the two hand cursors.
//
// Why a DLL at all: Microsoft.UI.Input.InputDesktopResourceCursor can only load
// a cursor that lives as a Win32 resource inside some module, and a .NET app's
// apphost cannot be given extra resources without hand-authoring the whole
// resource script for the exe (icon and manifest included). A tiny satellite
// module sidesteps that entirely.
//
// IDs must match CursorResource in PdfEditorApp/Controls/AppCursors.cs.

1 CURSOR "hand_open.cur"
2 CURSOR "hand_closed.cur"
